{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCoset","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionMurphy"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.existsUnique_isDistinguished_mem_coset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.existsUnique_isDistinguished_mem_coset","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionCosetExists.lean#L171-L189","doc":"**Mathas, Proposition 3.3** — the transversal statement.\n\n`D_μ` is a complete set of right coset representatives of `S_μ` in `S_n`: every coset\ncontains a distinguished element, and only one.\n\nThe length half — `ℓ(w·d) = ℓ(w) + ℓ(d)` for `w ∈ S_μ`, `d ∈ D_μ`, which is what gives\n`T_{wd} = T_w T_d` — is\n`CompositionMinimal.length_mul_eq_add_of_isDistinguished`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.exists_isDistinguished_mem_coset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.exists_isDistinguished_mem_coset","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionCosetExists.lean#L155-L169","doc":"**Existence**: every right coset of `S_μ` contains a distinguished element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.exists_shorter_of_not_isDistinguished","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.exists_shorter_of_not_isDistinguished","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionCosetExists.lean#L119-L145","doc":"**The shortening step.**  A non-distinguished `d` is not minimal in its coset:\nsome `v ∈ S_μ` strictly shortens it.\n\nThis is claim (C) of the probe, now proved.  With it, the minimal-length element of a\ncoset is distinguished, which is the existence half of Proposition 3.3.\n\nThe length computation is where the handedness dissolves: `sᵢ` is an involution, so\n`(sᵢ · d)⁻¹ = d⁻¹ · sᵢ`, and `length_inv` turns the left multiplication into the right\none that `invCount_mul_swap` already handles. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.exists_block_adjacent_descent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.exists_block_adjacent_descent","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionCosetExists.lean#L89-L117","doc":"**The shortening step's combinatorial half**: a non-distinguished `d` admits an\n**adjacent** transposition lying inside a block of `c`, across which `d⁻¹` descends.\n\n`sᵢ` is then in `S_μ` (its two labels share a block), and `ℓ(d⁻¹ · sᵢ) < ℓ(d⁻¹)` by\n`invCount_mul_swap` — which is `ℓ(sᵢ · d) < ℓ(d)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.le_of_adjacent_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.le_of_adjacent_le","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionCosetExists.lean#L59-L87","doc":"**A discrete descent exists**: if `f` weakly increases across every consecutive\npair inside `[p, q]`, then `f p ≤ f q`.\n\nStated as the contrapositive of what is wanted, because that is the direction the\ninduction runs. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.index_eq_of_between","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionCosetExists.index_eq_of_between","kind":"theorem","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionCosetExists.lean#L46-L57","doc":"**Blocks are intervals**: anything between two labels of one block is in that\nblock.  `lt_of_index_lt` gives the two inequalities; monotonicity of `index` does the\nrest. ","signatureChunk":0}]}